              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2. **Relatively soft**: Compared to transition metals, alkaline earth metals are relatively soft and can be easily deformed.",
            "start": 741,
            "end": 865
          },
          {
            "id": "p15",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "3. **Low density**: They have relatively low densities, with magnesium being the lightest.",
            "start": 866,
            "end": 956
          },
          {
            "id": "p16",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "4. **High melting and boiling points**: Alkaline earth metals have higher melting and boiling points than alkali metals.",
            "start": 957,
            "end": 1077
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "contains_error",
          "reason": "Magnesium is not the least dense alkaline earth metal; calcium has a lower density (~1.55 g/cm³ compared to magnesium's ~1.74 g/cm³). Additionally, if 'lightest' refers to atomic weight, beryllium (atomic mass ~9.01 u) is the lightest.",
          "errors": [
            {
